### Code

The destructor releases the resource when the object leaves scope, even if an exception unwinds the stack.

```cpp
class file {
  std::FILE* f_;
public:
  explicit file(const char* path)
    : f_(std::fopen(path, "r")) {}
  ~file() { if (f_) std::fclose(f_); }
};

// a is valid but unspecified after the move
std::string a = "hello";
std::string b = std::move(a);
```
